# Yalla 5roga — Project Context

## Project Overview

Yalla 5roga is a Flutter mobile app for planning group outings in Egypt: create groups, vote on plans, discover places, chat about events, and save drafts/bookmarks.

- Package: `yalla_5roga` (`pubspec.yaml` name)
- Display name: **Yalla 5roga** (`AppConstants.appName`)
- Monorepo sibling: `../backend` — Node.js + Express + Prisma + Neon PostgreSQL
- Product behavior SSoT: `../docs/PRODUCT_SCENARIOS.md` (also read `../AGENTS.md`)
- Entry: `lib/main.dart` → `AppDependencies.create()` → `lib/app.dart` `App`
- Firebase Auth (phone OTP, Google, Apple, email) + FCM behind repository adapters
- Neon PostgreSQL is the application data source of truth (via backend APIs)
- **No runtime mock/demo data layers** — repositories are always live API-backed

### Main technologies

Flutter + Dart, Provider (`ChangeNotifier`), GetX (`GetMaterialApp` navigation/snackbars/dialogs), Dio for the app API, `dartz` `Either` for failures, Equatable, SharedPreferences, Firebase Auth/Messaging, flutter_map + geolocator + Nominatim.

### Overall architecture

Feature-first Clean Architecture. **Every feature data path:**

```
UI Screen → Provider → Repository (Either) → Remote DataSource
  → ApiClient/Dio (live) | prefs cache (optional) | Firebase adapters (auth/push)
```

- `RepositoryFactory` builds API-backed repository implementations only
- Manual DI in `AppDependencies` (no get_it)
- Presentation must **not** import `ApiClient`, Dio, `http`, or Firebase packages
- No seed/demo fixtures; empty/error UI until the API responds

### Auth & push

- Firebase sign-in folded into `AuthRepository`; sync user to backend (`/api/users/sync`)
- FCM behind `PushMessagingRepository`; register device tokens with the backend
- Saved outings/places must use backend APIs (Neon), not prefs as sole SoT

### Modification rules

- Read `AGENTS.md` + `docs/PRODUCT_SCENARIOS.md` before behavioral changes
- Inspect and reuse existing layers before adding new ones
- Wire new app-wide providers in **both** `AppDependencies` and `App`
- Do not reintroduce mock/demo seed data layers
- Prefer existing shared widgets before new one-offs
